            <p class="lead">How does learning music change the brain?</p>
            <p>
                I study how musical training shapes brain structure, connectivity, and function, using multimodal
                MRI and structural connectomics. I'm a PhD candidate in computational neuroscience at the Sagol
                School of Neuroscience, Tel Aviv University, in Prof. Yaniv Assaf's lab.
                <br><br>
                Why music? I've played the trombone for over 20 years, which taught me first-hand how demanding
                it is to master a complex skill, and motivates my use of music as a model for studying how the
                brain learns.
